# The on-screen session. Not a desktop: an X server, a window manager for plugin
# editors, and nothing else.
#
# X11 rather than Wayland, and the reason is the plugins. Almost every Linux audio
# plugin editor - every LV2 X11 UI, every JUCE VST3, FBKSuppressor included - is an
# X11 window that expects to be embedded in the host. Under a Wayland compositor
# they reach the screen only through XWayland, if at all, and embedding is exactly
# the part that works least well. The compositor would buy nothing here anyway:
# there is one application and it is fullscreen.
xserver-xorg-core
xserver-xorg-video-all
xserver-xorg-input-all
xinit
x11-xserver-utils
openbox
unclutter
